[ENGLISH NOTICE — 영문 고지]

The core intellectual asset of this repository (`agentic-ontology-starter`) is the
**5-Stage Agentic Ontology Engineering Methodology** (comprising the 8-Phase Engineering
Lifecycle, 3-Layer OKF Wiki Architecture, Dual Property Graph Design, 8-Tool Modular MCP
& 2-Pass Agent Orchestration, and 4-Tier Lineage & Boundary Evaluation Framework),
together with all methodology guides (`methodology/`), executable notebooks (`notebooks/`),
industry reference templates (`industry_cases/`), prototyping playbooks (`PROTOTYPING_PLAYBOOK.md`,
`01_prod.md`), and reference source code (`src/`, `pipeline/`, `terraform/`).
All contents are provided strictly under **Non-Commercial Terms**.

1. Applicable Licenses (Dual Protection for Methodology & Source Code)
   - Core Methodology, Architecture Designs, Documentation, Notebooks & Templates
     (`methodology/`, `notebooks/`, `industry_cases/`, `*.md`):
     Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0
     International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0).
   - Reference Source Code & Pipeline Scripts
     (`src/`, `pipeline/`, `terraform/`, `config/`, `*.py`, `*.sql`, `*.tf`):
     Licensed under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0.

2. Permitted Non-Commercial Use
   - Personal learning, academic research, and non-commercial internal technical evaluation.

3. Strictly Prohibited Commercial Activities
   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may NOT:
   (1) Use the **5-Stage Ontology Methodology, deliverable specifications (D1.1–D5.5),
       architecture diagrams, notebooks, or source code** as part of any **paid consulting,
       system integration (SI) delivery, paid PoC/pilot engagement, commercial proposal,
       or client deliverable** for third-party organizations;
   (2) Embed, host, or operate the code or methodology within any commercial product,
       paid SaaS/cloud offering, or commercial production environment;
   (3) Modify, translate, repackage, or redistribute the methodology documents, notebooks,
       or code for paid training courses, workshops, or commercial publications.

4. Commercial Licensing & Collaboration Inquiries
   If you wish to use or adapt this methodology or codebase for a client engagement,
   commercial project, or enterprise deployment, please contact the author in advance:
   - Contact: Sean Jung <seanjung@google.com>

